{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Deprecation warnings\par
Deprecated functions make the compiler generate a warning when invoked. This is meant to invite users to update their source code. Should deprecation warnings be a problem, it is generally possible to disable them, typically with -Wno-deprecated-declarations for gcc or _CRT_SECURE_NO_WARNINGS in Visual.\par
Another method is to define LZ4_DISABLE_DEPRECATE_WARNINGS before including the header file. \par
}}
